From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Johannes Stein <johannesstein@freeze-dev.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 09:48:26 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 73/77] x86_64 win64 Exp: use the fdlibm algorithm of
 genmath.inc in the SSE2 routine (#41837 follow-up)

On x86_64-win64 (no extended type, so the x87 exp of rtl/x86_64/math.inc
is not used) fpc_exp_real has been a hand-written SSE2 routine since
2025: 2^k times a [6/6] Pade approximant P(x)/P(-x), with both
polynomials and the quotient rounded to double. That loses up to 2 ulp
(about 39% of random arguments are not correctly rounded, 8% are more
than 1 ulp off), and the range checks against log(2^1024) and
log(2^-1023) make Exp return +Inf for 709.7827128933840 (largest finite
result 1.797e308) and 0 for every argument below -709.09, where the
result is a subnormal down to -745.13. 3.2.x used the generic Pascal
fpc_exp_real of genmath.inc (fdlibm e_exp.c, error below 1 ulp) on
win64, so Exp, and with it Power, the hyperbolic functions and
everything built on them, changed in the last digits between 3.2.x and
trunk on win64 only. Other x86_64 targets use the x87 routine and are
unaffected.

Replace the routine by an SSE2 transcription of the genmath.inc code:
same constants, same argument reduction (r = hi - lo kept as two
doubles), same polynomial and the same operations in the same order, so
it gives bit-identical results to the generic version (no difference on
7.2 million arguments, all four rounding modes) and to 3.2.x on win64:
error below 1 ulp, subnormal results, overflow at 709.78271289338397
and underflow at -745.13321910194111. Overflow and underflow are again
computed as huge*huge and tiny*tiny as in genmath.inc, so an unmasked
overflow exception raises EOverflow on win64 again like in 3.2.x and on
the x87 targets (the SSE2 routine returned +Inf silently).

The new routine executes about 8% more instructions than the Pade one
(57.5 vs 53.0 per call under callgrind) and about 28% fewer than the
compiled genmath.inc version (79.3).

New test tests/test/units/system/texpacc.pp: arguments where the Pade
routine was 2 ulp off, subnormal results and the largest finite result.
